## Proof

Let $S = 1! + 2! + \cdots + 2009!$. We seek $\left\lfloor \dfrac{2010!}{S} \right\rfloor$.

**Rewrite.** Since $2010! = 2010 \cdot 2009!$,

$$\frac{2010!}{S} = \frac{2010 \cdot 2009!}{S} = \frac{2010}{S/2009!}.$$

Set $R = \dfrac{S}{2009!} = 1 + \dfrac{1}{2009} + \dfrac{1}{2009\cdot 2008} + \cdots + \dfrac{1}{2009!}$. Equivalently, factor out $1/2009$:

$$R = 1 + \frac{b}{2009}, \qquad b = \frac{2008!+2007!+\cdots+1!}{2008!} = 1 + \frac{1}{2008} + \frac{1}{2008\cdot 2007} + \cdots + \frac{1}{2008!}.$$

Thus
$$\frac{2010!}{S} = \frac{2010}{1+b/2009} = \frac{2010\cdot 2009}{2009+b} = \frac{4038090}{2009+b},$$
since $2010\cdot 2009 = 4038090$.

**Bounds on $b$.** Clearly $b > 1$ (it equals $1$ plus positive terms). Also
$$b = 1 + \frac{1}{2008} + \frac{1}{2008\cdot 2007} + \cdots < 1 + \frac{1}{2008} + \frac{1}{2008^2} + \cdots = 1 + \frac{1/2008}{1-1/2008} = 1 + \frac{1}{2007} < 1.0005.$$

**Upper bound (value $< 2009$):**
$$\frac{4038090}{2009+b} < 2009 \iff 4038090 < 2009(2009+b) = 2009^2 + 2009b = 4036081 + 2009b$$
$$\iff 2009 < 2009b \iff b > 1.$$
This holds. ✓

**Lower bound (value $\ge 2008$):**
$$\frac{4038090}{2009+b} \ge 2008 \iff 4038090 \ge 2008(2009+b) = 4034072 + 2008b$$
$$\iff 4018 \ge 2008b \iff b \le \frac{4018}{2008} \approx 2.001.$$
Since $b < 1.0005 < 2.001$, this holds. ✓

**Conclusion.** We have shown
$$2008 \le \frac{2010!}{1!+2!+\cdots+2009!} < 2009,$$
therefore
$$\left\lfloor \frac{2010!}{1! + 2! + 3! + \cdots + 2009!} \right\rfloor = \boxed{2008}.$$

